Z||000000||docprego||05-27-2001||02:33 AM||||I bought a 88 GT about 3 months ago.  It has sat in my garage ever since, not racking up more than 2 miles since I bought it.  I start it up once a week and take it for a spin around the block-that's it.<P>It has about 120K on the body and only about 3k on a new engine.<P>Body is just about mint as is the interior.<P>Has Driver's power lumbar option, factory sub (though not sure if it works well), sunroof, spoiler,power windows, locks and mirros, factory black honeycomb rims, not a single interior tear or stain.  Paint not faded.  Car looks great.<P>Here are photos of it:<BR> <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=112028&a=12401425&f=0" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=112028&a=12401425&f=0</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=112028&a=12364533&f=0" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=112028&a=12364533&f=0</A> <P>I paid too much for it, so how much should I ask if I sell it?  In other words what is a fair price to ask for this particular vehicle?<P>Thanks.<BR>docprego<BR><P>------------------<BR>docprego<BR> <A HREF="http://www.playitagain-games.com" TARGET=_blank>www.playitagain-games.com</A> <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Signature_2.jpg">   <BR>White 1988 GT<BR>Sunroof, Power lumbar seat, Factory sub||||reg||1
Z||000001||JSocha||05-27-2001||02:35 AM||||20 bucks and I'll take her off your hands!<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfiero||05-27-2001||03:11 AM||||Why are you selling it so soon after buying it?  You sounded pretty excited when you first bought it.....just curious.<P>BTW....whatever happened to that $300 '88 GT parts car you found?  LMK.<P> ||||reg||5
Z||000003||docprego||05-27-2001||03:21 AM||||Mr Fiero;<P>Too many cars, wife says one has to go!  (ok-truth is I am trying to fund the purchase of yet another car)<P>That parts car was sold before I ever had a chance, went back and it was gone...<P>Oh well, thanks for the reply.<BR><P>------------------<BR>docprego<BR> <A HREF="http://www.playitagain-games.com" TARGET=_blank>www.playitagain-games.com</A> <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Signature_2.jpg">   <BR>White 1988 GT<BR>Sunroof, Power lumbar seat, Factory sub||||reg||1
Z||000004||Old Lar||05-27-2001||06:32 AM||||Old Lar already has a white 88GT (less sun roof).  I'm glad the wife left before I got the Fiero habit.  It looks like its in good shape, I wouldn't take any dollar loss, if it is in as good shape as it appears.||||reg||1
Z||000005||87GTBro||05-27-2001||09:06 AM||||It looks like it is in pretty good condition.  Without driving though, I wouldn't be able to estimate how much to ask for it.  From the looks of it I would start at $3500 or $4000 and go up from there (depending on how much you paid for it and whether you want a profit and all that stuff).<P>It all depends on how much you value the car.  The new engine adds a whole bunch to the value.<P>Just my 2 cents.||||reg||1
Z||000006||docprego||05-27-2001||11:19 AM||||It is in as good a shape as the pictures make it look.  No dents, dings or scratches.<P>Exterior is just about perfect.  Only problem is a crack in the passenger side sail glass. <P>I do value the car, I searched for a nice one for a LONG time.<P>It drives great, starts right up.  A/C is strong and cold.<P>I'm thinking about asking about 5K, but not sure yet.....<P>ANY OFFERS??<P>Thanks all.<BR><P>------------------<BR>docprego<BR> <A HREF="http://www.playitagain-games.com" TARGET=_blank>www.playitagain-games.com</A> <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Signature_2.jpg">   <BR>White 1988 GT<BR>Sunroof, Power lumbar seat, Factory sub||||reg||1
Z||000007||Oreif||05-27-2001||12:17 PM||||I priced out the car via the Fiero Price Guide and the car comes to around $5950.00<BR>There is a $400 deduction for the mileage but since it has a rebuilt engine I did not deduct it. If I had the money, I'd pay $5k for it.||||reg||1
